<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;attempting again to use pre tags successfully; using them in conjunction with code tags seems not to display wide characters properly&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Yes, the issue with &lt;c&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;/c&gt; vs. &lt;c&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;/c&gt; tags and Unicode characters only working in the latter is a known issue on PerlMonks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;I'm still fishing for how I format this into homogenous-looking paragraphs.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have a look at the core module [doc://Text::Wrap]. Here's one way, I'm using the "paragraph mode" supported by [doc://$/] to read the file:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;c&gt;
use warnings;
use strict;
use open qw/:std :utf8/;
use Text::Wrap 'wrap';

open my $fh, '&lt;:raw:encoding(UTF-8)', '1.promises.txt' or die $!;
local $/ = '';
local $Text::Wrap::columns = 71;
while (&lt;$fh&gt;) {
	s/^\s+|\s+$//mg;
	if (/\A\w+\z/) {
		print ' ' x int( (71-length)/2 ), $_, "\n";
		next;
	}
	s/\n|\s{2,}/ /g;
	print wrap(' 'x5, '', $_), "\n";
}
close $fh;
&lt;/c&gt;
